// PILOT: first `SpriteSummon` ever authored as a real *player spell*. Every
// existing `SpriteSummon` RON is an NPC/monster trap or terrain-hazard
// scatter (custom/cursekeeper/trap.ron, custom/harvester/ensnaringvines_*.ron,
// custom/gigas_frost/icespike_*.ron, custom/dagon/seaurchins.ron): the
// variant always scatters copies of ONE `SpriteKind` across an area
// (common/src/states/sprite_summon.rs) -- there is no primitive to construct
// a walkable, multi-block building with floors and an interior, which is
// what the sheet literally describes ("a sturdy two-story tower... complete
// with floors and an interior").
//
// Ships instead as a small closed ring of `MagicalBarrier` sprites
// (common/src/terrain/sprite/mod.rs: a solid, height-3.0 sprite already
// flagged collidable alongside `GlassBarrier`/`OneWayWall`) around a chosen
// point -- a magical defensive perimeter/cover element a player can plant
// and fight from behind, not an enterable structure. Nothing shipped before
// this uses `MagicalBarrier` as a summoned effect. `anchor: Target` places
// the ring at the caster's selected point (the sheet's 9 m cast range)
// rather than around the caster themselves, which is the
// `SpriteSummonAnchor::Summoner` default every existing NPC-cast
// `SpriteSummon` uses instead. `del_timeout: None` matches "stands... until
// dispelled" -- no auto-expiry.
SpriteSummon(
    buildup_duration: 1.0,
    cast_duration: 0.4,
    recover_duration: 0.5,
    sprite: MagicalBarrier,
    del_timeout: None,
    summon_distance: (2.0, 3.0),
    sparseness: 0.0,
    angle: 360.0,
    anchor: Target,
    move_efficiency: 0.0,
    ori_modifier: 1.0,
    meta: (school: Some(Conjuration), source: Some(Arcane), cooldown: Some(45.0)),
)
